          "claim": "New tests never exercise the default (undefined) auto_comment path, which is the PR's core semantic",
          "description": "The fix's stated contract is \"when auto_comment is enabled (the default), every successfully triaged issue receives exactly one summary comment\". However, every test in triage-auto-comment.test.js sets pillars.triage.auto_comment explicitly (true or false) via mockGetConfigForRepo, so no test covers the path where auto_comment is undefined and the effective value comes from @gitwire/rules DEFAULT_CONFIG after merge. If the shipped default ever diverges from the assumed true (or the merge shape changes), the default-on behavior — the whole point of the fix — would regress without any test failing. A test asserting a comment is posted when the triage pillar config omits auto_comment would pin the default semantics.",
          "affectedPaths": [
            "packages/web/tests/unit/triage-auto-comment.test.js"
          ],
